      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "To illustrate the basic principles of multivariate BLUP, we follow the approach of Henderson and Quaas (1976), restricting our attention to the simplest of situations in which each of k traits has been measured once in each of n individuals. (For modifications necessary with missing data, see Henderson and Quaas 1976 and Mrode 1996.) The $ (nk) \\times 1 $ dimensional column vector of observations is denoted by the stack of univariate vectors,",
