    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "To obtain the mixed-model equations for the total vectors of fixed effects and breeding values, it only remains to specify the $ (nk) \\times (nk) $ covariance matrices $ \\mathbf{R} $ and $ \\mathbf{G} $ associated with the total vector $ \\mathbf{e}^T = (\\mathbf{e}_1^T, \\cdots, \\mathbf{e}_k^T) $ of residual errors and the total vector $ \\mathbf{a}^T = (\\mathbf{a}_1^T, \\cdots, \\mathbf{a}_k^T) $ of random effects.",
