      "content": "Let $\\mathbf{E}$ be the $k \\times k$ covariance matrix of within-individual environmental effects, with the $ij$th element being $\\sigma_E(i,j) = \\epsilon_{ij}$. In Kronecker product notation, the covariance matrix $\\mathbf{R}$ for the total vector of errors $\\mathbf{e}^T = (\\mathbf{e}_1^T, \\cdots, \\mathbf{e}_k^T)$ is",
